  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed replacement windows, by virtue of their materiality, would represent an unsympathetic and out of character addition that neither preserves nor enhances the significance of the listed building. It represents a visually harmful change to the character and appearance of the listed building, streetscene and wider conservation area and it has not been demonstrated that there would be a public benefit to outweigh any identified harm. Therefore the development fails to comply with Policies 53, 71 and 72 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of accurate, scaled drawings to assess the design, detailing and impact of the replacement windows on the historic interest and significance of the listed building, a full and accurate assessment cannot be carried out and the Local Planning Authority cannot be satisfied that the proposals would preserve or enhance the significance of the heritage asset(s). The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies 53, 71 and 72 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024), which require high quality, well detailed proposals supported by sufficient information to demonstrate that heritage significance will be conserved.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
